      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "TheaterEvent",
      "id": "6e87ee7471135dbb",
      "title": "«Nina Simone - 4 οκτάβες Ελευθερίας»",
      "description": "",
      "fullDescription": "The Arroyo Theater darkens and something in the air shifts. You're about to spend an evening with Nina Simone — not the woman herself, but the music, the legacy, the four octaves that contained multitudes. A tribute performance faces impossible standards. This one leans into that impossibility.\n\n\"4 Octaves of Freedom\" — the title captures what made Simone singular. That voice spanned everything from whispered intimacy to full-throated righteous fury, often within the same song. She was classically trained yet bluesy, technically precise yet emotionally unguarded. The tribute performer taking this on understands they're not imitating — they're channeling.\n\nThe audience for Nina Simone tribute shows brings particular expectations. You'll find people who know every album, who can tell you which version of which song they prefer. There are those discovering her through this entry point, led here by covers they've heard or recommendations they've received. And there are those for whom Simone represented something political, who heard freedom in those four octaves before anyone called it protest music.\n\nThe Arroyo Theater provides an appropriate setting — intimate enough that the emotional weight of this material lands, but substantial enough to contain the moments when the music opens up. Simone's catalog includes quiet devastation and soaring triumph, and both need room to breathe.\n\nIf you want a nostalgic greatest-hits cabaret, a comfortable trip through familiar melodies, this production likely has other ambitions. Simone's music was never comfortable. She made songs that forced audiences to feel things they'd rather avoid. A tribute that honors her would do the same. But if you're ready to experience what those four octaves carried — freedom, yes, but also pain, rage, beauty, and defiance — you're in for an evening that earns its title.\n\n| Info | Details |\n|------|---------|\n| **Date** | Friday, February 27, 2026 |\n| **Doors** | 20:00 |\n| **Show** | 21:00 |\n| **Venue** | Arroyo Theater, Athens |\n| **Price** | Check venue |\n\nFour octaves carried everything Nina Simone needed to say. The tribute attempts the same.",
